  "body": "A request has an associated origin (usually the origin of the client that made the request). Currently for foreign fetch we expect the foreign fetch event handler to pass this origin to respondWith to explicitly expose the contents of the response to that origin. But the origin of a request isn't actually exposed to javascript. I could add an `origin` or `clientOrigin` attribute to `ForeignFetchEvent`, but maybe it makes more sense to expose this directly for all `Request` instances?\n",
